<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-317 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>RETIMED 2026-11-13 (board): SpaceX ussf317 page now 'targeting Tuesday, November 17 ... four-hour launch window opens at 7:14 p.m. PT' (backup Wed Nov 18 8:54 p.m. PT) = 2026-11-18T03:14:00Z; LL2 NET same (Go, update 'Delayed to NET November 17 PST'). SpaceX timeline unchanged (MECO 2:26, sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:58). ZLA CARF 11/149-26 (Area A, for the Nov 16 slot) repeats the 11/116-26 polygon, so the 153.56 deg azimuth stands; no NOTAM yet for the Nov 18 03:14Z window. utc shifted by +256740 s; ECEF geometry unchanged.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-317 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 9.90 s, kick 3.657 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 16869 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.5564-0.001378*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
NEW 2026-11-12: SpaceX ussf317 page: &#x27;targeting Saturday, November 14 ... four-hour launch window opens at 7:55 p.m. PT&#x27; (backup Sun Nov 15 7:41 p.m. PT); LL2 NET 2026-11-15T03:55:00Z Go. Booster: 11th flight (B1100 per Next Spaceflight), OCISLY landing. ILLUSTRATIVE.
Published timeline (SpaceX ussf317, checked 2026-11-12): Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:58, entry burn 6:06-6:30, landing burn 7:52, landing 8:11. SECO, orbit, deploy NOT published (classified USSF mission).
INFERRED/ASSUMED: SECO-1 time and parking orbit are borrowed from the Starlink Group 15 analog via the USSF-627 config (LL2: drop zones exact fits with Group 15), not USSF-317 sources. Azimuth 153.56 deg from FAA/ZLA CARF NOTAM 11/116-26 Area A (identical to USSF-627&#x27;s polygon). File ends 2 revs after cutoff (deploy unpublished).
Target (see launch config): insertion 177 km, apoapsis 266 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 153.56 deg; payload 16869 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-18T03:14:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (SpaceX publishes no SECO, restart or deploy time for USSF-317 (national-security payload); propagated 2 revs on the inferred (Group-15-analog, borrowed from USSF-627 config) insertion orbit). From insertion T+519.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 88.93 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11191 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 177.22 km, osculating 174.5 x 268.9 km, i 68.265 deg.</description>
